# Backend Structure

## Stack

- Node.js
- NestJS (using Fastify adapter)
- Fastify
- Firebase (Firestore)
- Firebase Admin SDK

## HTTP Layer (Server)

The application must use Fastify as the HTTP engine via NestJS adapter.

- Use @nestjs/platform-fastify
- Express must NOT be used
- All HTTP handling must go through Fastify

## Database Layer (Firebase)

The application must use Firebase Firestore as the primary database.

- Use Firebase Admin SDK on backend
- No ORM (Prisma must NOT be used)
- Data access must be abstracted via repositories
- Collections must represent domain entities

## Architecture Layers

### 1. Modules Layer

Handles domain separation.

- transactions
- accounts
- debts
- investments

### 2. Domain Layer

Contains business rules.

- services
- rules
- validators
- entities (interfaces/types)

### 3. Analytics Layer

Handles intelligence.

- analysis services
- jobs
- insights

### 4. Infrastructure Layer

Handles technical concerns.

- firebase (config + client)
- repositories (Firestore access)
- queues
- external APIs
- http (Fastify configuration)

